\begin{lem}\label{thm:inexact:lb}%
	Let a constant \(c\in\R\), a sequence \(\seq{\gamma_j}[j\in\N]\searrow0\), and two bounded sequences \(\seq{u^j,z^j}[j\in\N]\) in \(\R^n\) be fixed, and for every \(j\in\N\) let \(\bar z^j\) be such that
	\[
		g(\bar z^j)+\innprod*{u^j}{\bar z^j-z^j}+\tfrac{1}{2\gamma_j}\|\bar z^j-z^j\|^2
		{}\leq{}
		\tfrac{c}{2\gamma_j}.
	\]
	Then, \(\seq{\bar z^j}[j\in\N]\) is bounded.
	\begin{proof}
		An application of Young's inequality on the inner product yields
		\[
		2\gamma_jg(\bar z^j)
		{}\leq{}
		c
		{}+{}
		\gamma_j\|u_j\|^2
		{}-{}
		(1-\gamma_j)\|\bar z^j-z^j\|^2.
		\]
		To arrive to a contradiction, up to extracting if necessary, suppose that \(0<\|\bar z^j\|\to\infty\).
		Since \(\liminf_{j\to\infty}{g(\bar z^j)}/{\|\bar z^j\|^2}>-\infty\) by \cite[Ex. 1.24]{rockafellar1998variational}, dividing by \(\|\bar z^j\|^2\) and passing to the limit leads to the contradiction \(0\leq -1\).
